What is a Smartphone?
Smartphones are multifunctional mobile devices that combine computing power, communication capabilities, and internet connectivity into a single handheld unit. These devices support a wide range of applications, from productivity tools and social media platforms to advanced photography and gaming experiences. Key components include high-resolution touchscreens, powerful processors, advanced camera systems, and long-lasting batteries.
